    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 80 Parkmore Drive is an exceptional 4 bedroom semi-detached, B energy rated, family home, ideally situated on one of the most sought after residential roads in Terenure. The property is in excellent condition and has been thoughtfully extended and remodelled by the current owners.\n \nThis Architecturally designed and light-filled property presents the lucky purchaser with a rare opportunity to acquire a well-proportioned family home. The ground floor comprises; a welcoming entrance hallway, a large living room, an open plan kitchen / living / dining area, guest wc and a utility room with access to the storage area.\n\nOn the first floor there are four bedrooms, with the principal bedroom benefitting from a generous en-suite and a walk-in wardrobe. A well appointed family bathroom completes the accommodation at this level. There is also potential to convert the attic (subject to the relevant planning permission) should your needs require.\n\nA description of this wonderful home would not be complete without mention of the fantastic gardens. To the front there is ample off-street parking and the provision of pedestrian access to the property via the storage area. To the rear there is a large and private garden that is laid mainly in lawn and benefits from a raised patio area. This space, which has been designed with great flair and imagination, is ideal for family dining and entertaining. Both the front and rear gardens are bordered by mature trees, hedging, flower beds and shrubbery.\n\nThe property is surrounded by a wealth of local amenities including well established local junior & senior schools and a wide range of sports clubs. The extensive recreational amenities and sporting facilities of both Bushy Park and Lakelands are within close proximity. The location of this home is fantastic, being within striking distance of a wealth of amenities, both social and essential, at nearby Terenure, Templeogue, Rathfarnham and Rathgar to include; an abundance of shops, bars and restaurants. There are also convenient local shops nearby at Greenlea, Fortfield and the KCR. Transport facilities are well catered for, with easy access to the M50, whilst nearby regular buses will take you into the City Centre and beyond.\nGreat taste and attention to detail make this a really special home. \n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 2.25m x 4.11m\nWelcoming and bright entrance hall with tiled flooring, ceiling coving, a radiator with cover, under-stair storage access, split stairs going up are lit up with natural light from a skylight.\n\nLiving Room - 3.62m x 7.51m\nThis bright, front-facing living space features laminate flooring, a fireplace, radiator, ceiling coving and double doors to the open living, dining and kitchen area.\n\nLiving Area - 4.75m x 4.74\nThis open plan living area is tiled with underfloor heating, includes a free standing wood-burning stove, recessed lighting, skylights and double doors to the rear garden.\n\nKitchen/Dining Area - 5.41m x 6.80m\nThis open plan kitchen and dining area is flooded with natural light from the 3 large skylights and tiled with underfloor heating, there are built in kitchen units, a stainless steel sink, tiled splashback, Induction hob, Samsung fridge-freezer, Neff oven and microwave, extractor fan, double doors with access to the rear garden and access to the utility room\n\nUtility Room - 2.58m x 1.83m\nThis room includes tiled flooring, a stainless-steel sink, Samsung fridge-freezer, Powerpoint washing machine, Indesit dryer, access to the fuseboard and boiler, built in units and shelving and a door to the garage.\n\nGarage - \nGarage with tiled flooring is accessible from the utility room and from the front.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.49m x 4.20m\nThis main double-bedroom facing the front features laminate flooring, and access to its own walk in wardrobe and en-suite bathroom.\n\nWardrobe - 1.50m x 2.05m\nWardrobe features a laminate flooring, built in shelving, recessed lighting and a sliding mirror closer door.\n\nEn-Suite - 1.35m x 2.62m\nEn-suite bathroom features fully tiled floor and walls, W.C, wash hand basin, radiator, recessed lighting and a shower cubicle with a handheld and rainfall shower heads.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.43m x 3.31m\nThis double bedroom facing the rear features laminate flooring, window and radiator.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.60m x 2.83m\nThis single bedroom facing the rear features carpet flooring, radiator and window.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.59m x 3.18m\nSingle bedroom facing the front featuring laminate flooring, radiator and window.\n\nBathroom - 2.70m x 1.86m\nBathroom faces the rear and includes tiled floor and walls, wash hand basin, W.C, bathtub with Triton T90xr electric shower, an led lit mirror, heated towel rail and recessed lighting.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Impressive 4 bedroom semi-detached property </li><li>Walk-in condition throughout, with an architecturally designed extension</li><li>Energy efficient, benefitting from a B3 rating </li><li>Ample off street parking to the front</li><li>Private and large rear garden </li><li>Potential to further extend the existing property, subject to PP</li><li>Gas fired central heating </li><li>Alarm System</li><li>A short stroll from Bushy Park and Lakelands</li><li>Close to a host of excellent local amenities, as well as primary and secondary schools </li><li>Well serviced by bus-routes and M50 access</ul>"
      },
